LibRaw 0.22.2: GetNormalizedModel() keeps `orig` in a function static, so two
LibRaw objects opening files on different threads (the editor and the export
queue here) can read each other's normalised model, and with it the colour
matrix and white level picked for it.

Backport of LibRaw 1a8fd32 ("changed (wrong) static to stack in
normalize_model", issue #876, in 0.22.3). Upstream's line context differs
(it adds the ILCE-7M5 table entry); the change is the same one line.

--- a/src/metadata/normalize_model.cpp
+++ b/src/metadata/normalize_model.cpp
@@ -400,7 +400,7 @@
       { SonyID_ILME_FX2,       "ILME-FX2"},
 };
 
-  static const char *orig;
+  const char *orig = NULL;
 
